In[1]:= (* ================================================================*)
(* Import wolfram files to compute equilibrium configurations *)
(* ================================================================*)

Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[],"..","wolfram","Geometry.wl"}]];
Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[],"..","wolfram","FourierBasis.wl"}]];
Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[],"..","wolfram","EnergyMagnetic.wl"}]];
Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[],"..","wolfram","BuildEnergy.wl"}]];
Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[],"..","wolfram","GroundState.wl"}]];
Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[],"..","wolfram","Plotting.wl"}]];

(* ================================================================*)
(* Equilibrium configurations for magnetic SkL *)
(* ================================================================*)

(*Build energy functional*)

emag=BuildMagneticEnergy[2,"Bloch"];

(*Load initial state*)

initialState=LoadMagneticEquilibrium["Bloch_N2_b0.5_xi0.88_Nz0.333333.txt"]

(*Calculate a new SkL configuration and save it*)

parameters={b->0.45,xi->0.88,lambda->500,Nx->1/3,Ny->1/3,Nz->1/3,alphaR0->0};

result=FindMagneticEquilibrium[emag,parameters,EquilibriumAnsatz[initialState],"Save"->True,"DMIType"->"Bloch"];

(*Plot the new SkL configuration*)

SkyrmionConfigurationPlot[LoadMagneticEquilibrium["Bloch_N2_b0.45_xi0.88_Nz0.333333.txt"]]

(*Calculate a field sweep*)

fieldSweep=ParameterSweep[emag,"Bloch",{xi->0.88,lambda->500,Nx->1/3,Ny->1/3,Nz->1/3,alphaR0->0},b,Range[0.5,0.3,-0.025],EquilibriumAnsatz[LoadMagneticEquilibrium["Bloch_N2_b0.5_xi0.88_Nz0.333333.txt"]]];

SkyrmionConfigurationPlot[LoadMagneticEquilibrium["Bloch_N2_b0.3_xi0.88_Nz0.333333.txt"],PlotPoints->150,ImageSize->550,Range->0.8]

(*Plot parameters over field sweep range*)

ListPlot[Table[{b,LoadMagneticEquilibrium["Bloch_N2_b"<>ToString[b]<>"_xi0.88_Nz0.333333.txt"][[1]]},{b,0.3,0.7,0.025}]]
ListPlot[Table[{b,a0/.LoadMagneticEquilibrium["Bloch_N2_b"<>ToString[b]<>"_xi0.88_Nz0.333333.txt"][[2]]},{b,0.3,0.7,0.025}]]

(* ================================================================*)
(*Import wolfram files to compute magnon dynamics*)
(* ================================================================*)

Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[],"..","wolfram","DynamicsProjection.wl"}]];
Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[],"..","wolfram","DynamicsMagnetic.wl"}]];

(* ================================================================*)
(*Calculate magnon dynamics with linearised LL equation*)
(* ================================================================*)

equilibrium=LoadMagneticEquilibrium["Bloch_N4_b0.5_xi0.88_Nz0.333333.txt"]

(*Plot the SkL configuration*)

SkyrmionConfigurationPlot[equilibrium]

(*Calculate magnon dynamics*)

dynamics=PrepareMagneticDynamics[equilibrium,"CheckInverse"->True];

modes=SolveMagneticModes[dynamics,{0,0,0},"FrequencyRange"->{0,6}];

(*Show low-energy magnon eigenfrequencies*)

modes["Frequencies"]

(*Plot real and imaginary parts of the magnon eigenfunction*)

MagnonEigenfunctionPlot[dynamics,modes,4,"Part"->"Both",ImageSize->600]
During evaluation of In[1]:= Geometry.wl
Affine geometry, reciprocal-lattice tools and coordinate transformations.
Function	Description
ee / EE	Return the affine basis and dual basis vectors.
metric / dualMetric	Return the affine metric and inverse metric tensors.
Vpuc	Return the primitive unit-cell area.
xi1 / xi2	Convert Cartesian coordinates to affine coordinates.
X / Y	Convert affine coordinates to Cartesian coordinates.
DotC / DotCn	Scalar products for covariant / contravariant affine components.
G / Gc	Return reciprocal-lattice vectors in affine components.
toCRT / toCRTc	Convert affine vector components to Cartesian components.
toAff / toAffc	Convert Cartesian vector components to affine components.
FT	Numerically compute a Fourier coefficient over one primitive cell.




During evaluation of In[1]:= FourierBasis.wl
Fourier-space field representations, reciprocal-space cutoff and reality constraints.
Function	Description
ConfigureFourierBasis	Set the reciprocal cutoff and magnetic representation (SixFold or General).
M	Return the active magnetic Fourier component M[n1,n2].
U	Return the elastic displacement Fourier component U[n1,n2].
MagneticVariables	Return the independent magnetic optimization variables.
ElasticVariables	Return the independent elastic optimization variables.
independentNodes	Return the independent reciprocal-space nodes inside the hexagonal cutoff.
hexagonNodeQ	Test whether a reciprocal node lies inside the finite hexagonal cutoff.




During evaluation of In[1]:= EnergyMagnetic.wl
Magnetic contributions to the dimensionless free-energy functional.
Function	Description
ExchangeEnergy	Exchange contribution.
BlochDMIEnergy	Bulk/Bloch DMI contribution.
NeelDMIEnergy	Interfacial/Neel DMI contribution.
AntiDMIEnergy	DMI contribution supporting antiskyrmions.
ZeemanEnergy	Zeeman coupling to a field along z.
MagnetostaticInfiniteEnergy	Magnetostatic energy for an extended sample with a Cartesian demagnetization tensor.
MagnetostaticFilmEnergy	Magnetostatic energy for a film of finite thickness.
MagnetostaticPeriodicEnergy	Magnetostatic energy for an infinite periodic multilayer.
ConstraintEnergy	Quartic penalty enforcing the fixed magnetization length.




During evaluation of In[1]:= BuildEnergy.wl
Assembly, symbolic simplification and caching of magnetic energy functionals.
Function	Description
BuildMagneticEnergy	Build or load a cached SixFold magnetic energy for a chosen cutoff and DMI type.
MagneticEnergyCacheFile	Return the cache path for a magnetic energy with a given cutoff and DMI type.




During evaluation of In[1]:= GroundState.wl
Ground-state minimization, equilibrium storage, loading and parameter continuation.
Function	Description
FindMagneticEquilibrium	Minimize the energy for fixed physical parameters and an initial ansatz.
SaveMagneticEquilibrium	Save an equilibrium configuration and metadata to results/equilibria.
LoadMagneticEquilibrium	Load a saved equilibrium by file name or by model parameters.
EquilibriumRules	Combine optimized variables and fixed parameters, e.g. for plotting.
EquilibriumAnsatz	Convert a compatible saved equilibrium into a FindMinimum ansatz.
ParameterSweep	Follow a metastable equilibrium branch while varying one parameter.
EquilibriumExistsQ	Check whether the expected equilibrium file already exists.




During evaluation of In[1]:= Plotting.wl
Real-space visualization of saved skyrmion equilibria and normalized magnetic magnon eigenfunctions.
Function	Description
MagnetizationAffine	Reconstruct the saved equilibrium magnetization in affine coordinates.
MagnetizationCartesian	Reconstruct the saved equilibrium magnetization in Cartesian components.
WZC	Construct the real-space Wigner-Seitz cell.
SkyrmionConfigurationPlot	Plot a saved equilibrium configuration with mz color map and in-plane magnetization arrows.
MagnonEigenfunctionCartesian	Reconstruct one normalized magnon eigenfunction in Cartesian components, including finite Bloch wavevector k.
MagnonEigenfunctionPlot	Plot the real, imaginary, or both parts of a magnon eigenfunction with common symmetric color scaling.
neighborVectors / Tpoint	Internal geometric helpers used to construct the Wigner-Seitz cell.




